1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,957
Long Test.

2
00:00:00,957 --> 00:00:04,979
A sharp, tearing sensation ripped through June's lower abdomen.

3
00:00:04,979 --> 00:00:09,294
It was so sudden, so violently intense, that her fingers went numb.

4
00:00:09,294 --> 00:00:11,518
The glass of water slipped from her hand.

5
00:00:11,518 --> 00:00:15,583
It hit the hardwood floor, shattering into dozens of jagged pieces.

6
00:00:15,583 --> 00:00:20,387
The sound echoed loudly in the massive, empty master bedroom of the Compton estate.

7
00:00:20,387 --> 00:00:23,270
June tried to take a step forward, but her knees buckled.

8
00:00:23,270 --> 00:00:28,101
A cold sweat instantly broke out across her forehead, sticking her hair to her skin.

9
00:00:28,101 --> 00:00:32,497
She collapsed onto the expensive Persian rug, her hands flying to her stomach.

10
00:00:32,497 --> 00:00:34,632
Her lungs forgot how to pull in air.

11
00:00:34,632 --> 00:00:40,023
The pain wasn't just a dull ache; it felt like a serrated blade twisting inside her organs.

12
00:00:40,023 --> 00:00:43,748
Her vision blurred at the edges, turning gray.She knew her body.

13
00:00:43,748 --> 00:00:45,516
She was a medical researcher.

14
00:00:45,516 --> 00:00:47,689
This was not a normal pregnancy cramp.

15
00:00:47,689 --> 00:00:49,558
Her vital signs were crashing.

16
00:00:49,558 --> 00:00:52,393
Her phone was on the nightstand, three feet away.

17
00:00:52,393 --> 00:00:53,767
It looked like a mile.

18
00:00:53,767 --> 00:00:57,352
Trembling violently, June dragged her body across the floor.

19
00:00:57,352 --> 00:01:03,777
The jagged pieces of the broken glass bit into her knee, but she couldn't even feel it over the agony in her abdomen.

20
00:01:03,777 --> 00:01:09,102
She reached up, her fingers blindly clawing at the nightstand until she knocked the phone down.

21
00:01:09,102 --> 00:01:11,054
The bright screen pierced her eyes.

22
00:01:11,054 --> 00:01:13,323
Her fingers were slick with cold sweat.

23
00:01:13,323 --> 00:01:16,079
She pressed the speed dial.Number 1.
Cole.

24
00:01:16,079 --> 00:01:17,400
The phone rang once.

25
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:25,161
June squeezed her eyes shut, her fingernails digging so hard into her palms that the skin broke.Please answer.Please.

26
00:01:25,161 --> 00:01:26,664
It rang a second time.

27
00:01:26,664 --> 00:01:29,719
Each second stretched out, heavy and suffocating.

28
00:01:29,719 --> 00:01:30,950
Then, a click.

29
00:01:30,950 --> 00:01:33,338
"What?"Cole's voice came through the speaker.

30
00:01:33,338 --> 00:01:34,576
It wasn't a greeting.

31
00:01:34,576 --> 00:01:36,055
It was a wall of ice.

32
00:01:36,055 --> 00:01:41,723
In the background, June could hear the clinking of champagne flutes and the smooth jazz of a live band.

33
00:01:41,723 --> 00:01:44,918
"Cole..."June gasped, her throat tight and dry.

34
00:01:44,918 --> 00:01:46,312
"Help me... the baby..."

35
00:01:46,312 --> 00:01:51,148
Before Cole could respond, a high-pitched, sweet voice drifted through the receiver.

36
00:01:51,148 --> 00:01:54,318
"Cole, who is it?We're going to be late for the red carpet."

37
00:01:54,318 --> 00:01:55,116
Alycia.

38
00:01:55,116 --> 00:01:56,638
June's stomach lurched.

39
00:01:56,638 --> 00:01:59,934
The pain spiked, sending a wave of nausea up her throat.

40
00:01:59,934 --> 00:02:04,274
"June," Cole said, his tone dropping into a low, impatient growl.

41
00:02:04,274 --> 00:02:09,393
"If this is your pathetic attempt to stop me from attending the gala, it's a terrible strategy."

42
00:02:09,393 --> 00:02:11,073
"No..."June choked out.

43
00:02:11,073 --> 00:02:14,670
She tasted something metallic in her mouth.Blood."I'm bleeding.

44
00:02:14,670 --> 00:02:16,957
Please."
"Stop acting," Cole snapped.

45
00:02:16,957 --> 00:02:22,090
She could almost see him adjusting his expensive cufflinks, annoyed by her existence.

46
00:02:22,090 --> 00:02:23,685
"You are perfectly fine.

47
00:02:23,685 --> 00:02:26,114
We are walking on stage in two minutes.

48
00:02:26,114 --> 00:02:28,223
Do not call this number again tonight."

49
00:02:28,223 --> 00:02:29,181
"Cole, wait-"

50
00:02:29,181 --> 00:02:30,370
The line went dead.

51
00:02:30,370 --> 00:02:32,699
The dial tone buzzed in the silent room.

52
00:02:32,699 --> 00:02:34,522
It sounded like a death sentence.

53
00:02:34,522 --> 00:02:36,589
June stared at the darkened screen.

54
00:02:36,589 --> 00:02:39,714
Her phone slipped from her weak grasp, landing on the rug.

55
00:02:39,714 --> 00:02:43,080
A sudden, terrifying warmth spread between her thighs.

56
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:49,208
June looked down.A dark, thick pool of red was soaking into the intricate patterns of the Persian rug.

57
00:02:49,208 --> 00:02:50,794
Blood.So much blood.

58
00:02:50,794 --> 00:02:52,841
A primal panic seized her chest.

59
00:02:52,841 --> 00:02:54,710
She was losing the ba by.

60
00:02:54,710 --> 00:03:00,773
With the last ounce of strength in her shaking fingers, she grabbed the phone again and dialed 911.

61
00:03:00,773 --> 00:03:03,022
"911, what is your emergency?"

62
00:03:03,022 --> 00:03:08,792
"Compton Manor..."June whispered, her voice barely leaving her throat."Hemorrhaging.Pregnant.Please hurry."

63
00:03:08,792 --> 00:03:10,030
She dropped the phone.

64
00:03:10,030 --> 00:03:11,992
Her head fell back against the floor.

65
00:03:11,992 --> 00:03:17,917
Across the room, the massive flat-screen TV was muted, playing a live broadcast of the charity gala.

66
00:03:17,917 --> 00:03:20,729
Through her half-closed eyes, June saw Cole.

67
00:03:20,729 --> 00:03:24,524
He looked breathtaking in his custom tuxedo.He was smiling.

68
00:03:24,524 --> 00:03:28,682
He was smiling down at Alycia, who had her arm wrapped tightly around his.

69
00:03:28,682 --> 00:03:31,964
Alycia wore a stunning white gown, looking like a bride.

70
00:03:31,964 --> 00:03:36,393
Cole's eyes held a tenderness that June had not seen in four years of marriage.

71
00:03:36,393 --> 00:03:38,025
The contrast was brutal.

72
00:03:38,025 --> 00:03:43,286
He was in the spotlight, holding another woman, while his wife was bleeding out on his bedroom floor.

73
00:03:43,286 --> 00:03:47,314
The wail of ambulance sirens pierced the night air, growing louder.

74
00:03:47,314 --> 00:03:50,309
Downstairs, the heavy oak doors banged open.

75
00:03:50,309 --> 00:03:52,209
Footsteps rushed up the stairs.

76
00:03:52,209 --> 00:03:55,561
Mrs. Lynch, the head housekeeper, appeared in the doorway.

77
00:03:55,561 --> 00:03:58,743
She didn't gasp in horror at June's pale face.

78
00:03:58,743 --> 00:04:00,900
Instead, her eyes darted to the floor.

79
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:03,984
"Good heavens," Mrs. Lynch muttered in disgust.

80
00:04:03,984 --> 00:04:05,747
"You've ruined the antique rug."

81
00:04:05,747 --> 00:04:08,296
Paramedics shoved past the housekeeper.

82
00:04:08,296 --> 00:04:11,276
They dropped a medical bag and knelt beside June.

83
00:04:11,276 --> 00:04:15,958
"Ma'am?Can you hear me?" a paramedic shouted, shining a penlight into her eyes.

84
00:04:15,958 --> 00:04:17,267
June couldn't speak.

85
00:04:17,267 --> 00:04:18,942
The room started to spin.

86
00:04:18,942 --> 00:04:20,747
They lifted her onto a stretcher.

87
00:04:20,747 --> 00:04:26,403
The movement sent a fresh wave of agony through her pelvis, and a silent tear slid down her temple.

88
00:04:26,403 --> 00:04:29,372
Inside the ambulance, the fluorescent lights flickered.

89
00:04:29,372 --> 00:04:34,099
"Blood pressure is tanking!" a medic yelled over the siren."Eighty over forty!

90
00:04:34,099 --> 00:04:37,506
Suspected ruptured ectopic pregnancy.Step on it!"

91
00:04:37,506 --> 00:04:39,995
The doors of the emergency room flew open.

92
00:04:39,995 --> 00:04:43,777
The wheels of the gurney rattled violently against the linoleum floor.

93
00:04:43,777 --> 00:04:47,064
The overhead lights passed by in a dizzying blur.

94
00:04:47,064 --> 00:04:50,904
Nurses swarmed her.Scissors cut through her blood-soaked clothes.

95
00:04:50,904 --> 00:04:54,346
"Where is the family?" a doctor demanded, holding a clipboard.

96
00:04:54,346 --> 00:04:55,701
"Where is the husband?

97
00:04:55,701 --> 00:04:58,220
We need consent for emergency surgery!"

98
00:04:58,220 --> 00:05:00,802
A nurse leaned over June."Mrs. Compton?

99
00:05:00,802 --> 00:05:01,996
Where is your husband?"

100
00:05:01,996 --> 00:05:04,231
June forced her heavy eyelids open.

101
00:05:04,231 --> 00:05:06,681
She looked at the nurse.Her lips trembled.

102
00:05:06,681 --> 00:05:10,378
"He..." June's voice was a broken whisper."He won't come."

103
00:05:10,378 --> 00:05:12,428
The doctor didn't wait."We're losing her.

104
00:05:12,428 --> 00:05:14,068
Get her to the OR now!"

105
00:05:14,068 --> 00:05:16,844
The heavy doors of the operating room swung shut.

106
00:05:16,844 --> 00:05:19,400
A mask was clamped over her nose and mouth.

107
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:22,844
The sweet, chemical smell of anesthesia filled her lungs.

108
00:05:22,844 --> 00:05:26,730
Her last conscious thought was the sound of Cole hanging up the phone.

109
00:05:26,730 --> 00:05:30,413
Hours later, the rhythmic beeping of a heart monitor woke her.

110
00:05:30,413 --> 00:05:31,784
June opened her eyes.

111
00:05:31,784 --> 00:05:37,038
The hospital room was dark, lit only by the streetlights of New York City filtering through the blinds.

112
00:05:37,038 --> 00:05:38,761
Her abdomen felt hollow.

113
00:05:38,761 --> 00:05:43,038
A dull, throbbing pain radiated from her surgical incisions.

114
00:05:43,038 --> 00:05:44,961
The room was completely empty.

115
00:05:44,961 --> 00:05:46,295
There were no flowers.

116
00:05:46,295 --> 00:05:49,080
There was no husband sitting in the chair beside her bed.

117
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:51,360
A nurse walked in to check her IV drip.

118
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:53,500
She offered June a look of deep pity.

119
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:55,738
"Mrs. Compton," the nurse said softly.

120
00:05:55,738 --> 00:06:01,270
"We tried calling the emergency contact number listed in your file several times.A Mr. Compton.

121
00:06:01,270 --> 00:06:02,805
He... he didn't answer."

122
00:06:02,805 --> 00:06:05,699
June turned her head slowly to look out the window.

123
00:06:05,699 --> 00:06:08,784
The city lights blurred into streaks of gold and silver.

124
00:06:08,784 --> 00:06:14,570
She didn't cry.The tears were gone, replaced by a freezing, solid block of ice in her chest.

125
00:06:14,570 --> 00:06:15,885
She closed her eyes.

126
00:06:15,885 --> 00:06:19,555
The June who loved Cole Compton had died on that operating table.
